+## Rotating the password
+
+To change the `password` without signing everyone out, pass a list with the new password first and the old one after it:
+
+```js
+const session = await useSession(event, {
+  password: [process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD, process.env.SESSION_PASSWORD_OLD],
+});
+```
+
+The first password seals every session, and every password in the list (in order) can unseal one. A cookie sealed with an older password is resealed with the first one on the next request, keeping its `id` and `createdAt`. Sessions read from the session header are never resealed.
+
+Remove the old password once `maxAge` has elapsed and no session sealed with it can still be valid. Keep the list short: each extra password costs a key derivation whenever a token cannot be unsealed. A compromised old password keeps being accepted for as long as it stays in the list.
+
 ## Get Data from a Session
 
 To get data from a session, we will still use `useSession`. Under the hood, it will use `getSession` to get the session.
